    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1953-p35.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Directly, \\[ f(x+2)=\\frac{(x+2)(x+1)}2. \\] Also \\(f(x+1)=\\frac{x(x+1)}{2},\\) so \\[ \\begin{gathered} \\frac{(x+2)f(x+1)}x\\\\ =\\frac{(x+2)(x+1)}2. \\end{gathered} \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
      "hints": [
        "Write explicit formulas for both \\(f(x+2)\\) and \\(f(x+1)\\)",
        "The factor \\(x\\) in \\(f(x+1)=\\frac{x(x+1)}{2}\\) cancels in one choice"
      ],
